      "writtenOn": "2025-12-04T13:49:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not just let the host driver consciously disable SVM if pKVM is enabled, instead of emulating lack of PRS support?\n\nRather than adding more stuff to pkvm_update_iommu_virtual_caps(), it looks like we can eliminate the whole pkvm_update_iommu_virtual_caps() if pvIOMMU is enabled? For example, the below \"limit PASID to reduce the memory consumptions\" is not needed either?",
      "revId": "db040a4cb7cb7460fdd84701422c3a1048a9cb29",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "813b46d6_5bfe97f9",
        "filename": "arch/x86/include/asm/pkvm.h",
        "patchSetId": 30
      },
      "lineNbr": 198,
      "author": {
        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-04T14:12:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Why not just let the host driver consciously disable SVM if pKVM is enabled, instead of emulating lack of PRS support?\n\nMy idea was to have minimal changes in driver code to achieve this. There are multiple places in driver code where we would want to touch to achieve this. \n\n\u003e Rather than adding more stuff to pkvm_update_iommu_virtual_caps(), it looks like we can eliminate the whole pkvm_update_iommu_virtual_caps() if pvIOMMU is enabled? For example, the below \"limit PASID to reduce the memory consumptions\" is not needed either?\n\nFor 6.12, I wanted to keep nested disabled for simplicity. And I have removed the PASID restriction in another cl.\n\nSo would it be okay to keep this as is to avoid more code churn?",
      "parentUuid": "32824c40_a651ef8e",
      "revId": "db040a4cb7cb7460fdd84701422c3a1048a9cb29",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b7130d18_9d6805f7",
        "filename": "arch/x86/include/asm/pkvm.h",
        "patchSetId": 30
      },
      "lineNbr": 198,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-04T15:54:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, for 6.12 we can keep it, 6.12 is a mess anyway.\n\nFor 6.18, I assume the plan is not to carry over pkvm_update_iommu_virtual_caps() to it? It would be nice not to carry it over to 6.18.\n\nLooks like in 6.18 we\u0027d just need to patch intel_svm_check() to disable SVM, and nested_supported() to disable nesting?\n\nAlthough, looks like 6.18 also made PRS independent of SVM, so we\u0027d also need to patch a couple of places if we want to force disabling PRS?.. (Assuming that we really need to force disabling it in the first place.)\n\n\u003e And I have removed the PASID restriction in another cl.\n\nYou mean changing PKVM_MAX_PASID_BITS from 15 to 20 in aosp/3786921? But the below \"limit PASID to reduce the memory consumptions\" is still not removed?",
      "parentUuid": "813b46d6_5bfe97f9",
      "revId": "db040a4cb7cb7460fdd84701422c3a1048a9cb29",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e21ba97a_6c9bf894",
        "filename": "arch/x86/include/asm/pkvm.h",
        "patchSetId": 30
      },
      "lineNbr": 198,
      "author": {
        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-04T19:49:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e For 6.18, I assume the plan is not to carry over pkvm_update_iommu_virtual_caps() to it? It would be nice not to carry it over to 6.18.\n\u003e Looks like in 6.18 we\u0027d just need to patch intel_svm_check() to disable SVM, and nested_supported() to disable nesting?\n\nYeah you\u0027re right, we can do all from the host driver. I think there are couple other places which needs minor modifications, but should be doable as we would be anyways working on host code mostly.\n\n\u003e You mean changing PKVM_MAX_PASID_BITS from 15 to 20 in aosp/3786921? But the below \"limit PASID to reduce the memory consumptions\" is still not removed?\n\nAhh yes, sorry I misunderstood. I will make this conditional. I also need to not disable SLTS for pviommu, currently we disable Nested | slts. Since pviommu support second level, I need to make that conditional as well. I think I will modify this patch to include all those changes, since all those changes are in one place.",
      "parentUuid": "b7130d18_9d6805f7",
      "revId": "db040a4cb7cb7460fdd84701422c3a1048a9cb29",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "98d96f1e_3e1eb5a4",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/Kconfig",
        "patchSetId": 30
      },
      "lineNbr": 139,
      "author": {
        "id": 3484945
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-04T11:33:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "hmm: perhaps it would be better to let this config be enabled with PKVM since when comparing results on platform where we have the CONFIG_\\*PKVM\\* enabled but disabled pKVM via command line, the comparison will not be fair and misleading, WDYT?\n\nIf you agree it would be better to disable SVM in the code via `if (pkvm_enabled()` - probably it will be needed in multiple places.",
      "range": {
