    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a17007e_45696256",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/Kconfig",
        "patchSetId": 30
      },
      "lineNbr": 139,
      "author": {
        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-04T14:12:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is specific to 6.12. I 6.12 we don\u0027t have SVM enabled for our kernel anyways and this is just a safeguard to accidental enabling. I can definitely do it in code, but it might be a little bit more churn. And for 6.18, we will be not be doing this.\n\nI can add more comments to make it clear and explicit. Would it be okay to keep it like this for simplicity?",
      "parentUuid": "44c8b97b_a4a4bbd6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 139,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 139,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "db040a4cb7cb7460fdd84701422c3a1048a9cb29",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ec109f0_35f2d08e",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/Kconfig",
        "patchSetId": 30
      },
      "lineNbr": 139,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-04T20:33:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After a closer look at the host driver code, I see intel_svm_check() exists in 6.12 as well, and enabling PRQ (if ecap_prs() is set) is quite independent of enabling SVM (if VTD_FLAG_SVM_CAPABLE is set).\n\nSo, if in 6.18 we plan to just disable SVM at runtime in intel_svm_check() if pKVM is enabled, and actually we can easily do the same in 6.12 as well, why not just do that in this patch, instead of forcing disabling INTEL_IOMMU_SVM at compile time? (That is independent of disabling ecap_prs.)",
      "parentUuid": "7a17007e_45696256",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 139,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 139,
